  - **The `state` string is stale right after recheck.** forceRecheck writes `m_nativeStatus.state` but never calls `updateState()`. `state()` returns `m_state`. updateState is called only from updateStatus (the state_update_alert, posted every `RefreshInterval`, default 1500 ms), reload, moveStorage and similar. So an info call immediately after recheck can return the pre-check string (e.g. `stoppedDL`) for up to about one refresh interval.
  - **`progress` and `amount_left` are also unreliable right after recheck.** `progress()` uses `isChecking()` on the forced cached state and returns `m_nativeStatus.progress`, which forceRecheck did not reset. `amount_left` = `total_wanted - total_wanted_done`, both stale.
